Subject: merge EGL vendor configuration from UAPI directories
Source: Nex downstream patch for libglvnd v1.7.0
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on adding a /run tier upstream

Add /run/glvnd/egl_vendor.d to the compiled-in default EGL vendor config
directory list, between the existing /etc and /usr/share tiers, and merge
the three default tiers by JSON basename. libEGL previously scanned each
default directory independently, so a vendor file installed under both
/etc/glvnd/egl_vendor.d and /usr/share/glvnd/egl_vendor.d with the same
basename loaded twice instead of the higher tier replacing the lower one.
Collect the highest-priority file for each basename across /etc, /run, and
/usr/share, then load the retained files in bytewise basename order. An
empty file or a symlink to /dev/null in a higher tier still claims the
basename, so it masks a same-named file in a lower tier even though it
fails to parse once loaded.

Leave the __EGL_VENDOR_LIBRARY_FILENAMES and __EGL_VENDOR_LIBRARY_DIRS
environment overrides on their upstream, unmerged behavior: the former
remains an exclusive list of exact JSON files, and the latter remains an
exclusive, ordered directory list scanned one directory at a time with no
basename deduplication across directories.

